  <!-- Proyecto Destacado: Carburo -->
  <article aria-labelledby="carburo-title">
    <header>
        <h2 id="carburo-title">Carburo — Smart fuel management</h2>
        <p>Final-year undergraduate project &amp; mobile and web ecosystem</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p>
        <strong>Carburo</strong> is a comprehensive platform designed to help users optimise their fuel spending, with real-time information on filling stations and price changes, as well as detailed consumption and refuelling records.
      </p>

      <section aria-label="Components of the Carburo ecosystem">
        <article>
          <h3>Native mobile application (main final-year project)</h3>
          <p>
            The core of my final-year Software Engineering project. Developed natively for Android, it includes geolocation, fuel-type filtering, visual price comparisons and fuel-efficiency analysis for registered vehicles.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Web platform and complementary services</h3>
          <p>
            Complementary development that extends the ecosystem to the web, allowing users to view statistical summaries and interactive filling-station maps, and to manage profiles from any browser.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <h3>Architecture and technologies</h3>
      <p>
        The ecosystem uses a modular architecture based on decoupled REST services:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Android SDK</li>
        <li>Java</li>
        <li>Spring Boot</li>
        <li>PostgreSQL</li>
        <li>REST API</li>
        <li>Docker</li>
        <li>Git / GitHub</li>
      </ul>

