  <!-- Proyecto: Infraestructura Web Segura -->
  <article aria-labelledby="infra-title">
    <header>
        <h2 id="infra-title">Secure and automated web infrastructure</h2>
        <p>Master's Degree in Web Engineering project</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p>
        Development of a complete infrastructure-as-code (IaC) environment for the coordinated, secure deployment of web applications in virtualised and cloud environments. The system provides automated provisioning, isolated networks, perimeter firewalls, containers and HTTPS certificate management.
      </p>

      <h3>Technology stack</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>OpenStack</li>
        <li>Terraform</li>
        <li>Ansible</li>
        <li>Linux (Debian/Ubuntu)</li>
        <li>Docker &amp; Compose</li>
        <li>Security &amp; HTTPS</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>

  <!-- Proyecto: Sitio Web Personal ECW -->
  <article aria-labelledby="ecw-title">
    <header>
        <h2 id="ecw-title">Personal and academic website (ECW)</h2>
        <p>Web Standards and Computing</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p>
        This website was developed following the principles of the <em>Web Standards and Computing</em>course. Built with Eleventy and Nunjucks, it separates responsibilities using semantic HTML5, external CSS and the cascade, with W3C validation as a development goal.
      </p>

      <h3>Technologies and standards</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Semantic HTML5</li>
        <li>CSS3 / Cascade</li>
        <li>Eleventy (11ty)</li>
        <li>Nunjucks</li>
        <li>WCAG accessibility</li>
        <li>W3C validation</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
